        "id": 1074628
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-04-19T06:30:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nothing in android should be requiring sudo access -- if you want to do something special, you should probably be ingesting a target-files package, then regenerating the image with releasetools, not mounting it.\n\nOr modifying it on the device (though I imagine you might need to wipe some state in data and/or reboot to make things appear as preinstalled)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 174,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 4
      },
      "revId": "492d7382f5cae6b365d9fb3f3673798df7a2e127",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "34554d2f_a297da03",
        "filename": "tests/PackageUpdate/build-image/run_build.bash",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1235686
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-04-27T13:22:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for your comment.\nAs our condition, we receive the image of new Android from Google directly due to no build environment for new Android before formal release.\nIf we can convert from image to target-files package and add test applications into target-files package with releasetools, we can do what we want without sudo.\nWe\u0027re checking releasetools,but we don\u0027t find anything yet.\n\nAnyway, we have other idea without sudo.\nWe try to mount and add test applications on Android device instead of Linux host PC.\nIf we are succeeded in it, we\u0027ll update patch set",
      "parentUuid": "19a3d843_9e261654",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 174,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 4
      },
      "revId": "492d7382f5cae6b365d9fb3f3673798df7a2e127",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0f4ef311_731b8d93",
        "filename": "tests/PackageUpdate/build-image/run_build.bash",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1235686
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-04-30T16:17:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Regarding previous my comment,  I\u0027d like to share the detail.\n\nIn my understanding, we need to have build environment to create target-files package by \"make dist\". But we have no AOSP build environment for new Android before formal release.\nInstead we receive the image files from Google directly.\nSo we need the tool to convert from image files to target-files package and add test applications into target-files package.\nWe\u0027re seeking it in releasetools, but we don\u0027t find yet.\n\nAs other idea, we try to add test applications into image files on Android device instead of Linux host PC.\nIn current implementation, we convert from image file to ext4 by using simg2img.\nAnd we mount ext4 in Linux host PC and add test applications into it.\nThen we need root privileges for mount command.\nSo we use \"sudo\".\nIn new idea, we push ext4 into Android device and mount ext4 there.\nWe can have root privileges with \"adb root\" command.",
      "parentUuid": "34554d2f_a297da03",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 174,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 4
      },
      "revId": "492d7382f5cae6b365d9fb3f3673798df7a2e127",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6c959f7a_a970709d",
        "filename": "tests/PackageUpdate/build-image/run_build.bash",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074628
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-04-30T22:25:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e In my understanding, we need to have build environment to create target-files package by \"make dist\". But we have no AOSP build environment for new Android before formal release.\n\nThis seems strange -- why are you testing a device that you don\u0027t have a build environment for? Are you trying to test the P developer preview? For test scripts in the tree you should be able to expect to be able to build the tree.",
      "parentUuid": "0f4ef311_731b8d93",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 174,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 4
      },
      "revId": "492d7382f5cae6b365d9fb3f3673798df7a2e127",
